 fork so you have around 30 people  trying to manage  how to contribute so in this first  conference we decide two things first  that we want to translate the text  and the data sets that are used in the  in the book  because they're not they're useful not  only for the book but for teaching art  and also which infrastructure we were  going to use  so we use mainly github and slack in  github we have our fork of the book  we have a repository with all the  documentation of the project  and the repository for the package  and we have responsibilities edgar  was leading the development of the  package  but i was involved with the taking care  that we didn't break the  the repository and i was involved with  the translation  and coordinating the whole process so  github is very useful for translation  because you can have like  both versions of the task and reviewers  can  put comments in between so they can make  suggestions how to improve the  translation  and slack was also very useful while we  can organizes  but also because of polls because there  we have to make  made many decisions about how we are  going to translate some stuff  for example we have empty cars  we have two translated cars and we can  state cars in three different ways in  spanish  so we have to decide altos coches or  carlos  so autos one and now we have emmett  and there's some other very difficult  stuff to decide for example we have the  pipe  and in spanish all nouns has a  grammatical gender so we have to decide  if the pipe was going to be  masculine or feminine so we made a poll  and everyone voted that  a pipe was masculine except me because  for me the pipe was a she  so now i have to like change all my mind  about how i thought about the pipe  so we decided uh that we want to  translate the text and the data sets and  for the text there was there were  previous experiences that were very  helpful and for example the  the carpentries have has translated some  lessons to spanish  and th